-- title:
--   Raynaud normal form for rank-q F-vector space schemes
-- statement:
--   Let $R'$ be a commutative ring which is a local domain, a discrete valuation ring, of characteristic zero; let $p$ be a prime and $r \neq 0$ a natural number, and let $F$ be a finite field with $\#F = p^{r}$. Assume $p^{r}-1$ is a unit of $R'$. Let $\chi : F^{\times} \to R'^{\times}$ be a homomorphism of multiplicative groups and $\iota : F \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\,R'$ a ring homomorphism such that the residue of $\chi(l)$ equals $\iota(l)$ for every $l \in F^{\times}$. Let $B$ be a commutative ring which is a Hopf algebra over $R'$, finite and free as an $R'$-module with $\operatorname{finrank}_{R'} B = p^{r}$, and let `fv` be an `FVectStructure F R' B`: a map $l \mapsto \mathrm{act}\,l$ from $F$ to coalgebra-compatible $R'$-algebra endomorphisms of $B$ with $\mathrm{act}\,1 = \mathrm{id}$, $\mathrm{act}(ab) = \mathrm{act}\,a \circ \mathrm{act}\,b$, and, in the convolution monoid on $R'$-algebra endomorphisms of $B$, $\mathrm{act}\,0 = 1$ and $\mathrm{act}(a+b) = \mathrm{act}\,a \cdot \mathrm{act}\,b$. Then there are elements $X_{0},\dots,X_{r-1} \in B$, indexed by `Fin r`, and $\delta_{0},\dots,\delta_{r-1} \in R'$ such that for all $i$ and all $l \in F^{\times}$ one has $(\mathrm{act}\,l)(X_{i}) = \chi^{p^{i}}(l)\cdot X_{i}$, that $X_{i}^{p} = \delta_{i} \cdot X_{i+1}$ with the index $i+1$ taken cyclically in `Fin r`, that $\delta_{i}$ divides $p$ in $R'$, that the counit of $B$ kills each $X_{i}$, and that the $R'$-subalgebra of $B$ generated by the $X_{i}$ is all of $B$.
--
--   This is the existence half of Raynaud's structure theorem for finite flat $F$-vector space schemes of rank $q = p^{r}$ over a base in which $q-1$ is invertible and which carries the fundamental character $\chi$: the augmentation ideal decomposes into eigenmodules for the $\mathrm{Frobenius}$ orbit $\chi, \chi^{p}, \dots, \chi^{p^{r-1}}$, and generators in those eigenmodules satisfy the cyclic relations $X_i^p = \delta_i X_{i+1}$ with $\delta_i \mid p$. It is used to pin down Hopf orders inside such algebras and to produce normal-form models in the inertial analysis of finite flat group schemes.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_HopfAlgebra_FVect_exists_generators_normalForm_of_finrank_eq_card.lean

